        "title": "[Feature] Add support for custom path-mapping rules in getFileExtension",
        "body": "getFileExtension relies entirely on static pathname regexes to extract file extensions. However, many API file URLs do not expose the extension in the path segment (e.g., they utilize redirects, file parameters like ?file=image.png, or rely on content-disposition headers).\n\nProposed Solution:\nAllow extensions to register custom filename/extension resolvers or define explicit mapping rules to handle URL path segment variations.\n\nSource Reference:\npackages/media-core/src/mime.ts#L140-L162",
